Aim: To install Ansible and create roles that automatically install Git, PostgreSQL and Apache.
Steps to perform
1. Open Ubuntu terminal.
2. Update and upgrade packages:
   sudo apt update
   sudo apt upgrade
3. Install the required repository package:
   sudo apt install -y software-properties-common
4. Add the Ansible repository:
   sudo add-apt-repository --yes --update ppa:ansible/ansible
5. Install Ansible:
   sudo apt install -y ansible
6. Configure the locale:
   sudo apt install -y locales
   sudo locale-gen en_US.UTF-8
   export LANG=en_US.UTF-8
   export LC_ALL=en_US.UTF-8
7. Verify the installation:
   ansible --version
8. Open the Ansible configuration directory:
   cd /etc/ansible
   ls -la
9. Edit the inventory file:
   sudo nano /etc/ansible/hosts
10. Add:
    localhost ansible_connection=local
11. Save and close the file.
12. Create the roles directory:
    sudo mkdir -p /etc/ansible/roles
    cd /etc/ansible/roles
13. Create three Ansible roles:
    sudo ansible-galaxy init prerequisites
    sudo ansible-galaxy init postgresql
    sudo ansible-galaxy init apache
14. Verify the directory structure:
    sudo apt install -y tree
    tree /etc/ansible/roles
15. Configure the prerequisites role:
    sudo nano /etc/ansible/roles/prerequisites/tasks/main.yml
    
    
    Add the Git installation task from your manual.
16. Configure the PostgreSQL role:
    sudo nano /etc/ansible/roles/postgresql/tasks/main.yml
    
    
    Add tasks to install PostgreSQL and start its service.
17. Configure the Apache role:
    sudo nano /etc/ansible/roles/apache/tasks/main.yml
    
    
    Add the Apache installation task.
18. Create the main playbook:
    sudo nano /etc/ansible/stack.yml
19. Enter:
    ---
    - hosts: localhost
      become: true
      roles:
        - prerequisites
        - postgresql
        - apache
20. Save the file and execute:
    cd /etc/ansible
    sudo ansible-playbook -i hosts stack.yml
21. Verify Git:
    git --version
22. Verify Apache:
    apache2 -v
23. Check PostgreSQL:
    sudo systemctl status postgresql
24. Verify the database cluster:
    pg_lsclusters
25. Test PostgreSQL:
    sudo -u postgres psql -c "SELECT version();"
